    <!-- Coach tips on the plan screen -->
    <plurals name="coach_not_started">
        <item quantity="one">Your plan starts tomorrow. Get some sleep and lay out your shoes.</item>
        <item quantity="other">Your plan starts in %1$d days. Easy runs until then are fine, but nothing hard.</item>
    </plurals>
    <string name="coach_race_week">Race week. Keep runs short and easy, sleep well, and don\'t try anything new on race day.</string>
    <string name="coach_taper">You\'re tapering. Running less now is how your legs get fresh for race day, so resist adding miles.</string>
    <plurals name="coach_missed">
        <item quantity="one">You missed a run in the past week. Don\'t double up to catch up. Just pick the plan up where it is.</item>
        <item quantity="other">You missed %1$d runs in the past week. Don\'t try to make them up. Pick the plan up where it is, and if this keeps happening, ask your assistant for a plan with fewer days.</item>
    </plurals>
    <string name="coach_easy_too_fast">Your easy runs have been well ahead of their target pace. Slowing down builds endurance with less risk of injury, and keeps your legs fresh for the hard days.</string>
    <string name="coach_long_run_today">Long run today. Start slower than feels natural, and bring water if you\'ll be out over an hour.</string>
    <string name="coach_rest_day">Rest day. Recovery is when your body adapts to the training.</string>
    <string name="coach_behind">%1$d of %2$d runs done so far. Don\'t try to make up the old ones: follow the plan from this week, and if it keeps slipping, ask your assistant to rebuild it from where you are now.</string>
    <string name="coach_on_track">On track: %1$d of %2$d runs done so far. Keep it up.</string>
    <string name="coach_finished">Race day has passed. Congratulations! Import a new plan when you\'re ready for the next one.</string>
